---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<Layout><main id="main"><section class="hero wrap"><p class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot"></span> A little companion for your Mac</p><h1>Your agents.<br/><span>A glance away.</span></h1><p class="intro">Stay in flow while your agents do their thing.<br class="desktop"/> Claude and Codex, right in your Mac’s notch.</p><div class="release"><span class="store"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="23" height="23" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M17.1 12.6c0-2 1.6-3 1.7-3.1-1-1.5-2.6-1.7-3.2-1.7-1.4-.1-2.6.8-3.3.8-.7 0-1.7-.8-2.9-.7C7.9 7.9 6.5 8.8 5.7 10c-1.6 2.8-.4 6.9 1.1 9.1.7 1.1 1.6 2.3 2.8 2.2 1.1 0 1.6-.7 3-.7s1.8.7 3 .7 2-1.1 2.7-2.1c.8-1.2 1.1-2.3 1.2-2.4-.1 0-2.4-.9-2.4-4.2ZM14.9 6.3c.6-.8 1.1-1.9 1-3-.9 0-2.1.6-2.8 1.4-.6.7-1.2 1.8-1.1 2.9 1.1.1 2.2-.5 2.9-1.3Z"/></svg><span><small>Coming soon to the</small>Mac App Store</span></span><p>Native macOS app. Made for your flow.</p></div><figure class="showcase"><div class="shot-top"><span class="status-dot"></span> LESS CHECKING. MORE CREATING.</div><img class="notch-shot" src={`${base}/images/notch.png`} alt="Quacktop’s expanded notch showing agent activity and provider quota windows" width="1064" height="484" fetchpriority="high"/><figcaption>Your next update is already up there.</figcaption></figure><div class="providers"><span>Built around the agents you use</span><div><strong class="claude">✳ <span>Claude Code</span></strong><span class="plus">+</span><strong>◉ <span>Codex</span></strong></div><small>More agents on the horizon.</small></div></section><section class="features wrap" id="features"><div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">IN THE LOOP. IN YOUR FLOW.</p><h2>A small space.<br/>A lot less switching.</h2><p>Let your terminal do the heavy lifting.<br/>Quacktop keeps the useful bits within sight.</p></div><div class="feature-grid"><article><span class="feature-number">01 / ACTIVITY</span><h3>Know who’s working.</h3><p>See your agents’ activity at a glance. Catch a finished reply or a request for attention without checking every terminal.</p></article><article><span class="feature-number">02 / USAGE</span><h3>Keep an eye on your limits.</h3><p>See reported Claude and Codex quota windows alongside recorded session usage. Less guessing before your next big task.</p></article><article><span class="feature-number">03 / ATTENTION</span><h3>A little nudge. Then back to it.</h3><p>Sounds and visual feedback bring important updates to you. Tune them to your workflow, with support for Reduce Motion.</p></article></div></section><section class="detail wrap"><div><p class="eyebrow">ALWAYS WITHIN REACH</p><h2>Just there.<br/>Until you need it.</h2><p>A compact view keeps activity and usage within sight. Expand it when you want the details, then get back to what you were making.</p><p class="fine">Screenshots show the current development build. Available features may vary by integration and permissions.</p></div><figure><img src={`${base}/images/compact.png`} alt="Quacktop’s compact notch with a working agent indicator and Claude quota" width="1064" height="76" loading="lazy"/></figure></section><section class="privacy-note wrap"><div class="privacy-symbol" aria-hidden="true">⌘</div><p class="eyebrow">YOUR MAC. YOUR WORK.</p><h2>Quiet by design.<br/>Local at heart.</h2><p>Your session data stays on your Mac by default. No Quacktop account, ads, or analytics. Optional provider connections go directly to the provider.</p><a class="text-link" href={`${base}/privacy/`}>Read the privacy policy <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></section><section class="closing wrap"><img src={`${base}/icon.png`} alt="" width="76" height="76" loading="lazy"/><h2>A little less switching.<br/>A little more shipping.</h2><p>Quacktop is coming soon to the Mac App Store.</p><a class="text-link" href="mailto:info@quackbyte.dev">Say hello <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></section></main></Layout>
